{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_051 (multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is our clear best at 0.715 acc, far exceeding singleprofile configs (~0.53) and the resnet50 multiprofile variant (0.632). The key winning factors are multiprofile + ViT-L image encoder + avgpool aggregation. Question: Can a transformer-based aggregation of multiple profiles outperform simple average pooling by capturing non-linear inter-profile interactions? This experiment (config_003) isolates that single variable—changing only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the proven scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, and concat fusion—making it the cleanest logical extension of our best result. Why now: With 5 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest direction is justified; transformer aggregation is the most likely architectural upgrade to push accuracy above 0.715. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_051 (4.49 GPU hrs) due to the transformer attention layers over profiles, likely ~6–8 GPU hours, which is affordable within our remaining budget."
}

